# Discord multilingual translation layer

Implement **one phase at a time**. Do not generate the entire project in a single pass. Do not continue to the next phase while the current one is failing.

## Product constraints

- No cloud translation APIs. Local TranslateGemma 4B 4-bit via oMLX only.
- Do not persist Discord message contents. SQLite stores IDs and sync metadata only.
- Never log raw Discord content or secrets.
- Keep Discord handlers thin. Keep model-specific code behind `TranslationProvider`.
- Keep SQLite access inside repositories.
- Every network call needs timeout/error handling. Every queued operation must be idempotent.
- Protect against stale message-edit results.

## Disk and RAM (Mac mini M4, 16 GB)

- Use only `mlx-community/translategemma-4b-it-4bit`. Never download 12B/27B or extra models.
- Keep a single copy of the weights in the oMLX model dir. Do not keep a duplicate Hugging Face cache.
- Bind the model server to `127.0.0.1` only.
- Prefer RAM-only inference. Do not enable an unbounded SSD KV cache.
- Abort large downloads if free disk would fall below ~15 GB.
- After each phase: `npm run build`, `npm test`, fix errors, summarize files, give exact manual verification commands.
